{
  "variants": [
    {
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> The firewall has logged our scan activity. Detection is useful context, not failure, but any additional checks now require coordination with the SOC.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> Decide how the alert should change the next scan pass."
    },
    {
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Kade Mercer:</b> The scan activity is visible in the edge logs, although the rate stayed below the block threshold. Decide whether that warning changes how far you push the map.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Kade Mercer:</b> Choose how you respond now that the edge can see the probes."
    },
    {
      "persona": "Hacktivist",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Lena Ortiz:</b> The edge alert does not tell us whether internal monitoring saw the earlier vendor-to-ticketing flow. That possible monitoring gap belongs in the questions we ask, not in the facts we claim.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Lena Ortiz:</b> Decide how to raise the visibility question without overstating what the alert proves."
    }
  ],
